Hi Ido,

These are not the reference manuals you are looking for.  The one you 
really want is actually here:

http://www.bioconductor.org/packages/2.11/bioc/html/OrganismDbi.html


The reason is because the OrganismDbi package is the software package 
behind the scenes that is doing all the work (it also documents how to 
use packages like Mus.musculus etc.).  In contrast, the Mus.musculus 
package itself is actually just a hollow shell that contains almost no 
information, code or documentation of it's own.  It just points to other 
packages that have all that and contains just enough information to 
allow OrganismDbi to find what it needs.

But now that you have pointed this shortcoming in the documentation out, 
I am going to put a reference to the OrganismDbi package in there for 
users to find when they click that link...

Thank you,


  Marc



